2. Use and self-hosting

Subject to these terms, the copyright owner grants individuals and
organizations a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to download,
copy, build, install, run, privately modify, and back up the Project for:

- Personal use and study, including local development and evaluation.
- Self-hosted chat for yourself, your household, a group or community whose
  members you admit, or your organization's own workforce. Members may
  access that instance and run project-provided clients to connect to it.
  The instance may serve its bundled web client in the normal course of
  providing that access.

An organization may use the Project for its own internal work, including
commercial work. You may pay for hosting infrastructure for a permitted
instance. The instance may be reachable over the internet if admission is
controlled by the operator and restricted to the intended members.

